# Round 6 summary (generated by `python -m selab.summary_r6`)

Real = LibriCSS 7-mic recordings (round-5 items). Panel = 48 items (2 per recording, 24 recordings; 36 overlapped).
CIs: 95% cluster bootstrap over recordings, 2000 resamples. Δ = method minus reference method on the same item. Holm: within the family of round-6 methods, per group and per comparison (vs unprocessed; vs round-5 DS). A bootstrap p of 0.000 means < 1/2000.

Steering: R5 tracker = round-5 running SRP-PHAT (re-implemented on causal frames); track+hyst. = multi-candidate tracker, no speaker check; track+ECAPA = with enrolment speaker check; REF dir. = system-identification azimuth (oracle geometry, upper bound); blind whole-seg. = non-causal segment SRP-PHAT (as round-5 DS).

